---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';

const ogImage = new URL(`/og${Astro.url.pathname.replace(/\/$/, '')}.png`, Astro.site).href;

const grades = [
	{
		grade: 0,
		name: 'No functional limitations',
		desc: 'No symptoms and no limitations in everyday life related to the infection.',
	},
	{
		grade: 1,
		name: 'Negligible limitations',
		desc: 'You can perform all usual duties and activities, although you still have persistent symptoms, pain, depression or anxiety.',
	},
	{
		grade: 2,
		name: 'Slight limitations',
		desc: 'You occasionally need to avoid or reduce usual duties and activities, or spread them over time, due to symptoms. You can perform all activities without assistance.',
	},
	{
		grade: 3,
		name: 'Moderate limitations',
		desc: 'You are not able to perform all usual duties and activities due to symptoms, but you can take care of yourself without assistance.',
	},
	{
		grade: 4,
		name: 'Severe limitations',
		desc: 'You need assistance with activities of daily living: you are dependent on nursing care and/or assistance from another person due to symptoms.',
	},
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="Post-COVID-19 Functional Status (PCFS) scale: free online self-assessment"
			description="Find your PCFS grade in under a minute. The Post-COVID-19 Functional Status scale grades the functional impact of long COVID from 0 (no limitations) to 4 (severe limitations), with each step explained."
			ogImage={ogImage}
		/>
		<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "itemListElement": [
        {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://www.postviralrecovery.com/"},
        {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Tools", "item": "https://www.postviralrecovery.com/tools/"},
        {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Post-COVID-19 Functional Status scale", "item": "https://www.postviralrecovery.com/tools/pcfs/"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the PCFS scale?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "The Post-COVID-19 Functional Status (PCFS) scale is a simple ordinal scale proposed by Klok and colleagues in 2020 to measure how much everyday functioning is affected after COVID-19. It has five grades, from 0 (no functional limitations) to 4 (severe limitations, needing assistance with daily living). It has been translated into more than 25 languages and is widely used in long COVID research and rehabilitation."}
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What do the PCFS grades mean?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Grade 0: no limitations. Grade 1: symptoms persist but all usual activities can be performed. Grade 2: usual activities occasionally need to be reduced, avoided, or spread over time. Grade 3: not able to perform all usual activities. Grade 4: needing assistance with activities of daily living. Grades 2 and above generally indicate a level of limitation worth discussing with a clinician or rehabilitation service."}
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is the PCFS a measure of symptom severity?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "No. It deliberately measures functional consequences rather than symptoms. Two people with the same symptom list can have very different PCFS grades depending on how much their daily life is limited. For symptom-level detail, pair it with a symptom questionnaire; for fine-grained functional capacity in ME/CFS-type illness, the FUNCAP questionnaire is more detailed."}
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
		</script>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main id="main">
			<div class="tool-header">
				<a href="/tools" class="section-label tools">Tools</a>
				<h1>Post-COVID-19 Functional Status scale</h1>
				<p class="subtitle">PCFS: a 0–4 grading of how much daily life is affected</p>
				<p class="description">
					The PCFS scale was proposed by Klok and colleagues in 2020 as a common yardstick for functional status after COVID-19. It gives you a single grade from <strong>0 (no functional limitations)</strong> to <strong>4 (severe limitations)</strong>. It is widely used in long COVID research and rehabilitation, with versions in more than 25 languages.
				</p>
				<p class="description">
					Its strength is simplicity. It measures <strong>consequences for daily life</strong> rather than symptoms, so it works as a quick, repeatable tracking measure. Answer the four questions below to find your grade. It takes well under a minute.
				</p>
				<p class="description">
					Want more detail? The <a href="/tools/funcap/">FUNCAP questionnaire</a> profiles what 27 specific activities cost you, and the <a href="/tools/bell-scale/">Bell scale</a> gives a 0–100 functional rating. If your symptoms flare after activity, see the <a href="/tools/dsq-pem/">post-exertional malaise questionnaire</a>.
				</p>
				<div class="disclaimer">
					<strong>This is not a diagnostic tool.</strong> The PCFS grades the functional impact you report; it does not diagnose long COVID or measure symptom severity. Discuss your grade with your doctor. Based on: Klok FA, Boon GJAM, Barco S, et al. <em>The Post-COVID-19 Functional Status scale: a tool to measure functional status over time after COVID-19.</em> Eur Respir J. 2020;56:2001494 (CC BY-NC 4.0).
				</div>
			</div>

			<div id="flow" class="flow">
				<div class="flow-step" data-q="0">
					<p class="flow-question">1. Can you live alone without any assistance from another person?</p>
					<p class="flow-hint">For example: independently washing, dressing, eating, and using the toilet.</p>
					<div class="flow-answers">
						<button type="button" data-answer="yes">Yes</button>
						<button type="button" data-answer="no">No</button>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="flow-step" data-q="1" hidden>
					<p class="flow-question">2. Are there duties or activities at home or at work that you are no longer able to perform yourself?</p>
					<p class="flow-hint">Things you did before the infection that you now cannot do at all.</p>
					<div class="flow-answers">
						<button type="button" data-answer="yes">Yes</button>
						<button type="button" data-answer="no">No</button>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="flow-step" data-q="2" hidden>
					<p class="flow-question">3. Do you suffer from persistent symptoms, pain, depression, or anxiety related to the infection?</p>
					<p class="flow-hint">For example: fatigue, breathlessness, brain fog, loss of taste or smell, palpitations.</p>
					<div class="flow-answers">
						<button type="button" data-answer="yes">Yes</button>
						<button type="button" data-answer="no">No</button>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="flow-step" data-q="3" hidden>
					<p class="flow-question">4. Do you need to avoid or reduce your usual duties or activities, or spread them over time?</p>
					<p class="flow-hint">You can still do everything, but you have to pace, cut back, or plan around symptoms.</p>
					<div class="flow-answers">
						<button type="button" data-answer="yes">Yes</button>
						<button type="button" data-answer="no">No</button>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div id="results" class="results" hidden>
				<h2>Your PCFS grade</h2>
				<div class="total-score">
					<span id="grade-value">—</span>
					<span id="grade-name" class="total-score-label"></span>
				</div>
				<p id="grade-desc" class="score-interp"></p>
				<div class="results-buttons">
					<button type="button" id="restart-btn" class="back-btn">Start again</button>
				</div>
			</div>

			<section class="grade-table-section">
				<h2>The five PCFS grades</h2>
				<div class="grade-table">
					{grades.map(g => (
						<div class="grade-row" data-grade={g.grade}>
							<div class="grade-num">{g.grade}</div>
							<div>
								<p class="grade-name">{g.name}</p>
								<p class="grade-desc">{g.desc}</p>
							</div>
						</div>
					))}
				</div>
			</section>

			<div class="results-disclaimer">
				<h3>Using your grade</h3>
				<p>The PCFS is most useful tracked over time: the authors suggest recording it at discharge or diagnosis, and again at intervals such as 4–8 weeks and 6 months. A grade that is not falling over months is a concrete, communicable signal to raise with your GP or a long COVID service.</p>
				<p>Grades 2–3 generally indicate a level of limitation where rehabilitation support and pacing advice are appropriate; grade 4 indicates a need for care support. The scale is deliberately coarse, so a stable grade can still hide real change. Pairing it with a more detailed tool such as the <a href="/tools/funcap/">FUNCAP</a> or a <a href="/tools/trackers/symptom-diary/">symptom diary</a> gives you both the headline and the detail.</p>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<script>
const GRADES = [
	{ grade: 0, name: 'No functional limitations', desc: 'No symptoms and no limitations in everyday life related to the infection. If this changes, re-grade yourself. The scale is designed for repeat use.' },
	{ grade: 1, name: 'Negligible limitations', desc: 'You still have symptoms, but they do not stop you performing your usual duties and activities. Worth re-checking monthly: a move to grade 2 or above is a signal to seek support.' },
	{ grade: 2, name: 'Slight limitations', desc: 'You occasionally need to avoid or reduce usual activities or spread them over time. At this level, pacing advice and a structured symptom record start to be genuinely useful. Consider discussing support with your GP.' },
	{ grade: 3, name: 'Moderate limitations', desc: 'You are not able to perform all usual duties and activities, though you can care for yourself. This level of limitation warrants clinical support. A long COVID service or rehabilitation referral is worth asking about, and documenting your limitations helps.' },
	{ grade: 4, name: 'Severe limitations', desc: 'You need assistance with activities of daily living. This warrants active clinical involvement and care support. Documenting your functional status (this grade, plus a detailed tool such as FUNCAP) supports referrals and any benefits or insurance assessment.' },
];

const flow = document.getElementById('flow') as HTMLElement;
const steps = Array.from(flow.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.flow-step'));
const results = document.getElementById('results') as HTMLElement;

function showStep(n: number) {
	steps.forEach(s => { s.hidden = parseInt(s.dataset.q || '0', 10) !== n; });
}

function finish(grade: number) {
	const g = GRADES[grade];
	(document.getElementById('grade-value') as HTMLElement).textContent = String(g.grade);
	(document.getElementById('grade-name') as HTMLElement).textContent = g.name;
	(document.getElementById('grade-desc') as HTMLElement).textContent = g.desc;
	flow.hidden = true;
	results.hidden = false;
	document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.grade-row').forEach(row => {
		row.classList.toggle('active', parseInt(row.dataset.grade || '-1', 10) === grade);
	});
	results.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
}

flow.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
	const btn = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLButtonElement>('button[data-answer]');
	if (!btn) return;
	const step = btn.closest<HTMLElement>('.flow-step');
	const q = parseInt(step?.dataset.q || '0', 10);
	const yes = btn.dataset.answer === 'yes';

	// PCFS flowchart (Klok et al. 2020):
	// Q1 assistance needed -> 4; Q2 unable to perform activities -> 3;
	// Q3 no symptoms -> 0; Q4 needs to avoid/reduce -> 2, else 1.
	if (q === 0) { yes ? showStep(1) : finish(4); }
	else if (q === 1) { yes ? finish(3) : showStep(2); }
	else if (q === 2) { yes ? showStep(3) : finish(0); }
	else { finish(yes ? 2 : 1); }
});

document.getElementById('restart-btn')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
	results.hidden = true;
	flow.hidden = false;
	document.querySelectorAll('.grade-row.active').forEach(r => r.classList.remove('active'));
	showStep(0);
	flow.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
});
</script>

<style>
	.tool-header {
		padding-bottom: 1.5em;
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		margin-bottom: 2em;
	}
	.tool-header h1 { margin: 0.3em 0 0.1em; }
	.subtitle { color: rgb(var(--gray)); font-size: 1.05em; margin: 0 0 0.75em; }
	.description { margin-bottom: 1em; }

	.flow { margin-bottom: 2.5em; }
	.flow-step {
		border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		border-radius: 8px;
		padding: 1.5em 1.75em;
	}
	.flow-question { font-size: 1.15em; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 0.3em; line-height: 1.4; }
	.flow-hint { color: rgb(var(--gray)); font-size: 0.9em; margin: 0 0 1.25em; }
	.flow-answers { display: flex; gap: 0.75em; }
	.flow-answers button {
		font-family: inherit;
		font-size: 1em;
		font-weight: 700;
		padding: 0.65em 2.5em;
		border-radius: 5px;
		border: 1px solid var(--accent);
		background: none;
		color: var(--accent);
		cursor: pointer;
		transition: background 0.1s, color 0.1s;
	}
	.flow-answers button:hover { background: var(--accent); color: #fff; }

	/* Results */
	.results { padding-top: 0.5em; margin-bottom: 2.5em; }
	.results h2 { margin-bottom: 0.5em; }
	.total-score { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.6em; margin: 0.75em 0; }
	#grade-value { font-size: 3.5em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); line-height: 1; }
	.total-score-label { color: rgb(var(--gray-dark)); font-size: 1.3em; font-weight: 700; }
	.score-interp {
		font-size: 1em; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 1em;
		padding: 1em 1.25em; background: var(--accent-light);
		border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 4px;
	}
	.results-buttons { margin-top: 0.5em; }

	.grade-table-section h2 { margin-bottom: 0.75em; }
	.grade-table { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.6em; margin-bottom: 2em; }
	.grade-row {
		display: flex;
		gap: 1em;
		align-items: flex-start;
		border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		border-radius: 8px;
		padding: 0.9em 1.2em;
	}
	.grade-row.active { border-color: var(--accent); box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--accent-light); }
	.grade-num {
		flex: 0 0 auto;
		width: 1.9em; height: 1.9em; line-height: 1.9em;
		text-align: center;
		background: var(--tools-bg); color: var(--tools);
		border-radius: 6px; font-weight: 700;
	}
	.grade-row.active .grade-num { background: var(--accent); color: #fff; }
	.grade-name { font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 0.15em; }
	.grade-desc { margin: 0; font-size: 0.88em; color: rgb(var(--gray-dark)); line-height: 1.5; }

	.results-disclaimer {
		font-size: 0.88em; color: rgb(var(--gray-dark));
		border-top: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light)); padding-top: 1.5em;
		line-height: 1.6;
	}
	.results-disclaimer h3 { font-size: 1em; color: rgb(var(--black)); margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0.5em; }
	.results-disclaimer a { color: var(--accent); }
	.back-btn {
		background: none; border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
		padding: 0.6em 1.25em; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 0.95em;
		cursor: pointer; color: rgb(var(--gray)); font-family: inherit;
	}
	.back-btn:hover { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); }

	@media (max-width: 600px) {
		.flow-step { padding: 1.1em 1.2em; }
		.flow-answers button { flex: 1; padding: 0.65em 0; }
	}
</style>
